{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/155419-demonic-investments-for-a-vampire-spoilers-east-bay-sabbat-stay-out","id":155419,"title":"Demonic investments for a vampire (Spoilers, East Bay Sabbat stay out!)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-31T21:08:45-07:00","id":155419,"title":"Demonic investments for a vampire (Spoilers, East Bay Sabbat stay out!)","content":"I've got a Vampire PC, Remus, that's made a pact with a demon (he doesn't quite realized that's what it is). He sacrificed an innocent to it, and granted it him the ability to grow large spiky quills when he wishes.<br /> <br /> Other PCs have noticed something's up, and one of them is actively looking into exorcism, thinking that this might be a case of possession. It isn't. Because they had a pact at one point, the demon hangs around, trying to get more out of Remus. Also, it can hear through his ears as a side-effect of the pact.<br /> <br /> Although an exorcism won't work, I figure a direct attempt at banishing the demon (from Earth, or from Remus's presence) will prevent any further contact.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, <b>What might happen to the infernally-granted quills? Would Remus still have this gift, or would it be stripped away if the demon is banished? </b><br /> <br /> As a final note, this character is basically doomed. The Inquisition is building a case, and they're coming for him at the end of the story. The player has given me explicit permission to fuck over his character. If the other PCs are just too effective at rescuing their friend from the pitfalls of infernalism, then his reckless abuses of Obtenebration will get him instead. All I want is to time his downfall with the end of the story.<br /> <br /> (For rules context: This is a VtM game. I'm not using any Demon: the Fallen material. I've mostly been using this draft of Rites of the Blood as a resources for the demon and infernalism:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xn2Z_m4iWgew_QzE9VCNHeBaGQBP_uj3bMCDjB80yIQ/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xn2Z_m4iWgew_QzE9VCNHeBaGQBP_uj3bMCDjB80yIQ/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xn2Z_m4iWgew_QzE9VCNHeBaGQBP_uj3bMCDjB80yIQ/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xn2Z_m4iWgew_QzE9VCNHeBaGQBP_uj3bMCDjB80yIQ/edit </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> Additionally, there's some &quot;rule of cool&quot; and basic pop-culture understanding of evil forces tossed in. There has been no significant crossover with other official WoD splats. )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T21:54:46-07:00","id":155439,"title":"","content":"From everything that I recall from Book of Madness, the investments wouldn't go away if the demon is sent away -- unless the demon himself makes the quills grow every time, it's something he's already done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T15:00:28-07:00","id":155997,"title":"","content":"Well you could create some horribly contrived and torturous rite only to reveal that he can NEVER get rid of the demon unless it wants to leave and its having way too much 'fun' by manipulating the character, -well except at the moment inquisition gets him cutting the demons fun short and it might even help the player get away by creating a blatantly demonic &quot;miracle&quot; only to abandon him when its most deliciously evil to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T02:25:45-07:00","id":157682,"title":"","content":"He's given a way a chunk of his soul in exchange for those quills so unless the demon gives it back (nope) or the demon dies (again cant happen) he's stuck, it would, as it was stated above, take a Miracle to fix it.<br /> <br /> And lets face it, vampires who make deals with a demon usually don't get divine intervention unless its the flaming sword kind.<br /> <br /> Anyone that makes a pact with anything willingly should be treated harshly, they have messed up and it is not going to end will.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Test","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2374-happypig","name":"HappyPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2374_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T13:37:33-07:00","id":158221,"title":"","content":"Something related I've been wondering:<br /> <br /> What does giving up <i>part</i> of one's soul actually mean for a person?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T14:39:52-07:00","id":158300,"title":"","content":"It means there's wiggle room inside the person for a demon to get a foothold. If we're going on the excellent chapter dedicated to Infernalism in Book of Madness, Revised, then it's less a matter of giving away &quot;part&quot; of your soul, but slowly transferring ownership or control of your soul away from yourself and to the demon. Like a tug-of-war competition with your soul in the middle, except you're getting a weaker grip or less of a foothold while the demon is getting stronger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T07:23:05-07:00","id":162407,"title":"","content":"Tremere had a Level-Four ritual (in Player's Guide to Low Clans) for which they could conjure a demon and make exchanges for power. One of the possibilities is trading parts of the vampire's soul. P. 174<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the demon wants nothing or the price is too high, the caster can offer his soul in trade. Every dot of Road the caster forsakes from his maximum rating converts into one dot of a Discipline, Thaumaturgy path or Attribute or three dots to distribute among Abilities or Backgrounds. For example, a thaumaturge who pledges three dots can never have a Road rating higher than 7. Disciplines obtained through this ritual always manifest as corrupted in some way: infernal Creo Ignem creates baleful green or stinking sulfurous fire, while infernal Obtenebration might permanently stain its user\u2019s eyes inky black. Backgrounds obtained with this ritual do not manifest immediately, arriving via amazing twists of fate and coincidence at the rate of one dot per week. Such Backgrounds invariably result from the suffering (or death) of another. Once an infernalist pledges his first point of Road, he can never reach Golconda. </div> </div> </div>So, you get the idea of what giving up part of one's soul can mean for a vampire. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/78-bloodarmor","name":"BloodArmor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar78_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T10:56:33-07:00","id":162527,"title":"","content":"Either way, it's generally a Very Bad Idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}